# BikeNoCo project rules

## Stack and constraints
- Native iOS app: SwiftUI + MapKit + CoreLocation, iOS 17.0 deployment target, Swift 5.
- NO third-party packages (no SPM, no CocoaPods). Use Apple frameworks only. If something seems to need a library, write the small piece yourself or ask first.
- The Xcode project is generated by XcodeGen from `project.yml`. Never hand-edit `BikeNoCo.xcodeproj`. Edit `project.yml` instead.
- After adding, removing, or renaming any source file, run `xcodegen generate` before building. New files will not compile until you do.

## Code layout
- `BikeNoCo/Models` data types, `BikeNoCo/Services` logic and I/O, `BikeNoCo/ViewModels`, `BikeNoCo/Views`.
- Routing and navigation code goes in `BikeNoCo/Routing/` (graph, search, maneuvers, navigation engine).
- Routing code must be pure Swift: import Foundation and CoreLocation only. No SwiftUI, UIKit, or MapKit in `BikeNoCo/Routing/`, so it stays unit-testable and fast.
- Existing data model: `BikeRoute` (in `Models/BikeRoute.swift`) with `FacilityType`, optional `lts`, `streetName`, `bikewayName`, `paths: [[CLLocationCoordinate2D]]`. `.recommendedRide` routes are RideWithGPS overlays, not infrastructure; exclude them from the routing graph.
- `lts` is nil for all trails and all Loveland data. Treat nil carefully; do not assume nil means high stress.

## Verify your own work
Pick an available simulator once with `xcrun simctl list devices available` and reuse it.

Build:
```
xcodegen generate && xcodebuild -project BikeNoCo.xcodeproj -scheme BikeNoCo -destination 'platform=iOS Simulator,name=<SIMULATOR>' build | tail -30
```

Test (once the BikeNoCoTests target exists):
```
xcodegen generate && xcodebuild -project BikeNoCo.xcodeproj -scheme BikeNoCo -destination 'platform=iOS Simulator,name=<SIMULATOR>' test | tail -40
```

- A task is not done until the build succeeds and tests pass. Fix errors yourself before reporting back.
- Every routing/graph change gets unit tests using small synthetic graphs, not live ArcGIS data.

## Specs
- The design source of truth is `docs/routing-and-navigation.md`. The earlier `docs/smart-route-planner.md` covers the loop planner and is still valid for that feature.
- Task prompts live in `docs/tasks/`. Do only what the current task asks; note follow-ups instead of doing them.

## Style
- Match existing code style: `@MainActor final class ...: ObservableObject` for view models, `async/await` for I/O, small focused files.
- Distances in meters internally; format to miles/feet only at the UI layer.
- No force unwraps in new code except in tests.
